<Layouts.app flash={@flash}>
  <section id="security-page" class="border-b border-border bg-card/45">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:px-8">
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold text-primary">
        <.icon name="hero-shield-check" class="size-4" /> Security and data handling
      </span>
      <h1 class="mt-6 max-w-4xl text-balance text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-6xl">
        A controlled replay boundary, described without compliance theater.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">
        Silent Regression is being built for an invite-only alpha. This page separates the intended data flow from safeguards that must pass verification before customer prompts, outputs, or credentials are accepted.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl space-y-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-warning/25 bg-warning/10 p-6 sm:p-8">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <span class="grid size-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-xl bg-warning/15 text-warning-foreground">
            <.icon name="hero-wrench-screwdriver" class="size-5" />
          </span>
          <div>
            <h2 class="font-semibold">Current implementation stage</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
              The public application collects prospect information only. Provider credentials and monitored workflow data will not be enabled for design partners until tenant isolation, application-level credential encryption, redaction, and deletion behavior are implemented and tested in later tasks.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.72fr_1.28fr]">
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-primary">
            Planned data flow
          </p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
            Managed replay, not production surveillance.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-4">
          <article class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
            <div class="flex gap-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-primary">01</span>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold">Your team supplies a bounded test workflow</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
                  Prompt, frozen context, representative cases, requested provider/model configuration, and explicit output contracts—not a production traffic feed.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
            <div class="flex gap-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-primary">02</span>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold">Silent Regression performs the replay</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
                  Scheduled runs require a customer-provided OpenAI or Anthropic credential stored by the service. No SDK or library runs inside your production environment.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
            <div class="flex gap-4">
              <span class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-primary">03</span>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold">Results stay within the invited workspace</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">
                  Captured outputs, rule evidence, provenance, and review history will be scoped to verified workspace memberships and excluded from public pages.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t border-border pt-12">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-primary">
            Release gates
          </p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
            What must be true before a pilot receives access.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
          <li class="flex gap-3 rounded-xl bg-muted/50 p-5 text-sm leading-6">
            <.icon name="hero-key" class="mt-0.5 size-5 shrink-0 text-primary" />
            Credentials are encrypted at the application layer, revocable, and never returned to the browser.
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3 rounded-xl bg-muted/50 p-5 text-sm leading-6">
            <.icon name="hero-user-group" class="mt-0.5 size-5 shrink-0 text-primary" />
            Cross-workspace access is rejected by explicit adversarial tests.
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3 rounded-xl bg-muted/50 p-5 text-sm leading-6">
            <.icon name="hero-eye-slash" class="mt-0.5 size-5 shrink-0 text-primary" />
            Secrets, prompts, contexts, and outputs are redacted from logs and operational metadata.
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3 rounded-xl bg-muted/50 p-5 text-sm leading-6">
            <.icon name="hero-trash" class="mt-0.5 size-5 shrink-0 text-primary" />
            Credential revocation and customer-data deletion behavior are verified.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-sidebar p-7 text-sidebar-foreground sm:p-9">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">No certifications are claimed.</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-6 text-sidebar-foreground/65">
          The private alpha is not currently represented as SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, PCI, or otherwise certified. Security and procurement requirements raised by design partners will be recorded as product evidence, not converted into premature badges.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layouts.app>
